      "sourceTextSha256": "ee29a34e0d63731d6cb383412657c611b706bbe2310f7e903a2175a269370e75",
      "text": "Day 2 · Antigua city tour. Founded in 1543 as Santiago de Guatemala, the third capital of the country, Antigua lies in the Panchoy valley between the volcanoes of Agua, Acatenango and Fuego. By the mid-18th century it had some 25 churches, numerous convents and a cathedral built in 1680; in 1773 the Santa Marta earthquakes destroyed much of the city and the capital moved to present-day Guatemala City. Its finest museum is the city itself, best discovered on foot. Overnight at Hotel Villa Colonial. (B)",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1MfFMYvTkHizz2y7XQmdC0cIjNgd0tmbg",
